WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:11.480
iPhone forensics requires careful preservation, authorized acquisition, knowledge of iOS architecture, artifact interpretation, timeline correlation, and disciplined reporting.

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.500
Investigators must understand what each artifact can support and what it cannot support.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.280
Strong investigations begin with documentation.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:33.820
Device model, iOS version, patch level, power state, lock state, visible notifications, network state, SIM or eSIM context, custody, tools, methods, and acquisition scope all matter.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:40.200
Early handling decisions can affect evidence availability, so preservation is not separate from analysis.

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:42.900
Architecture shapes access and meaning.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:57.440
App sandboxing, data protection, Secure Enclave concepts, app containers, shared containers, keychain concepts, backups, iCloud sync, and application behavior all influence what data exists and how it can be interpreted.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:03.820
A missing artifact may reflect protection, scope, retention, sync behavior, or tool support.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:09.480
A present artifact may reflect local action, account state, or background processing.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.500
Analysis should correlate artifacts across sources.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:28.640
Messages, calls, Safari records, notifications, media, EXIF data, location traces, app records, backups, iCloud records, endpoint telemetry, network logs, and witness statements can reinforce or challenge each other.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:34.540
Timestamps need careful normalization, and conclusions should separate observation from interpretation.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:37.400
The goal is not to extract everything possible.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:45.380
The goal is to preserve relevant evidence, protect privacy, document uncertainty, and support defensible investigative conclusions.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:52.160
Good iPhone forensics is technical, but it is also disciplined, privacy-aware, and humble about what the evidence can prove.
